REVISE

REASONS
- **[Blocking] Contract enforcement is not active in production execution path**.  
  The new guard exists in `DefaultToolExecutor`, but I could not find any production construction site passing it through. In the runtime composer, `DefaultToolExecutor(...)` is still created without `scope_guard`, so `decide_tool_in_scope` is never consulted during normal agent runs. That means “dispatch-boundary enforcement” is implemented but not actually wired.  
  - Affected files: [`packages/tools/src/disco/tools/executor.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/tools/executor.py), [`packages/tools/src/disco/agent_server/runtime.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/agent_server/runtime.py)

- **[Blocking] Governed-set appears incomplete and mismatched to actual tool IDs, creating bypasses**.  
  `DANGEROUS_TOOLS` uses `bash` and `exec` while the registry includes mutating tools like `shell_exec`, `code_exec`, `file_append`, and `file_str_replace` (plus `shell_*` process tools), which are omitted and therefore treated as ungoverned utilities. That bypasses scope gating and violates intent for dangerous mutators.  
  - Affected files: [`packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/enforce.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/src/disco/core/contract/enforce.py), [`packages/tools/src/disco/tools/registry.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/tools/registry.py)

- **[Non-blocking] Test suite does not validate end-to-end activation of guard wiring**.  
  The added tests show core decisions and executor behavior under injected guard, but they do not confirm that the live runtime path actually constructs the executor with a contract-aware `scope_guard`. Also missing regression cases for omitted mutator aliases.  
  - Affected files: [`packages/core/tests/test_contract_enforce.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/tests/test_contract_enforce.py), [`packages/tools/tests/test_executor_contract_scope.py`]( /var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/tests/test_executor_contract_scope.py)

REQUIRED_REVISIONS
- Wire `scope_guard=ContractScopeGuard.for_contract(...)` (or equivalent) into the production executor construction path in `agent-server` runtime.
- Reconcile govern/deny taxonomy with actual tool IDs and include all mutating tools in scope enforcement (or derive from tool metadata):
  - include `file_append`, `file_str_replace`, `shell_exec`, `code_exec`, and shell process tools if they are mutable.
  - replace/remove stale entries like `bash`/`exec` unless they are real registered tool names in this codebase.
- Add regression tests for:
  - executor created by runtime uses active `ContractScopeGuard` and actually blocks out-of-scope dangerous calls end-to-end.
  - denial of missing mutator tools (`file_append`, `file_str_replace`, `shell_exec`, etc.) in a scoped phase.

